      "rev_n_1_83c6b9_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_83c6b9_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_83c6b9",
        "thought_text": "Dynamic Programming Approach with Correct State Transition\n\nThe current dynamic programming approach seems incorrect because it does not properly account for the constraints on runs of length at most \\( k \\). Instead, we should use a different approach that considers valid permutations directly. We can use a recursive method with memoization to count permutations that satisfy the condition. This approach ensures that we only consider valid sequences and avoid counting invalid ones.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_83c6b9_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_0cd09a7cc4",
        "created_at": 1794505907.4724405
      },
      "rev_n_2_fbad06_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_fbad06_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_fbad06",
        "thought_text": "Dynamic Programming Approach",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_fbad06_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_18c7dbcf25",
        "created_at": 1794505984.4601953
      },
      "rev_n_3_7ad678_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_7ad678_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_7ad678",
        "thought_text": "Thought-1 (revised): Dynamic Programming with Memoization\n\nTo fix the error, we need to apply the `@lru_cache(None)` decorator to the `dp` function within the `count_permutations` function. This ensures that memoization is applied correctly to the recursive calls made by `dp`. By doing this, we avoid the `NameError` and ensure that the dynamic programming approach works as intended.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_7ad678_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_ee0f1ae03a",
        "created_at": 1794505998.2649884
      },
